// Feature: a warband's rules version, shown and switched (2026-11-03). Code: routes ((app)/warbands, (app)/warbands/[id]
// form action rules, api/v1/warbands/[id]/rules), services/warbands (setRules), services/rules (rulesLabel),
// services/warband-choices (rulesChoices), services/rules-load (manifest preview), lib/ui/rules/RulesTag.
views {
  dynamic view warband_rules {
    title 'Warband rules version'
    description '''
      **Every warband shows the rules it is built for ("1.0.1", "1.0.2 (Carcass Front)", "1.0.2 (Preview)"), and its
      owner picks them when creating it and may switch them later.**

      **Decisions** (asked in chat and approved 3 Nov 2026)
      - The label is the core version, then the chosen expansions' names in brackets; a set marked `preview` in its
        manifest (not an official release) gets the preview tag.
      - Creation offers every loaded core and every expansion whose chain reaches one (an expansion on an expansion too).
      - The owner may switch any time outside a campaign; fighters and kit stay, and what the new rules lack shows as
        problems (not refused). In a campaign seat the campaign's rules apply, so it is locked.
    '''
    user -> fl.app.web.areas 'owner: Warband panel → Change rules'
    fl.app.web.areas -> fl.app.services.warbandService 'setRules (PUT /api/v1/warbands/[id]/rules)'
    fl.app.services.warbandService -> fl.app.services.rulesService 'load the chain; the faction must be in it'
    fl.app.services.warbandService -> fl.app.repos 'update rules_set, rules_expansions (version check)'
    fl.app.repos -> fl.app.warbandTables 'warbands'
    fl.app.services.warbandService -> fl.app.services.auditService 'record warband.rules'
    user -> fl.app.web.areas 'any page with warbands'
    fl.app.web.areas -> fl.app.services.warbandService 'warband views with their rules label'
    fl.app.services.warbandService -> fl.app.services.rulesService 'rulesLabel: version, expansion names, preview'
  }
}
